{
 "slice": "campaign-close-dispositions",
 "dated": "2026-08-14",
 "decisions": [
  "D-24",
  "D-72",
  "D-97",
  "Amendment E"
 ],
 "correction": {
  "one_sentence": "A number the walk refused to produce stops being published as a number a rule produced: a refused transition's outcome fields carry STRUCTURAL_ZERO with the walk's own refusal as the reason, instead of a MEASURED zero with the refusal sitting one key away as a bare string.",
  "sites": [
   "src/calculator/survival/outcome_state.py::outcome_quantity -- the two answers a refusal makes different, in one expression, so the ledger and the projection that publishes its numbers cannot disagree about one transition",
   "src/calculator/program/views/receipt.py::_outcome / _refusal -- the three panels publish their outcome fields through that one verdict"
  ],
  "why_it_had_no_symptom": "StructuralZero.read() is 0.0 and the branch is only reached on a zero, so no published number moves. What moves is what the payload SAYS about those numbers, which is the whole of umbrella criterion 1's emission clause.",
  "not_touched": "AttackerOutcome and ObjectiveFold still carry plain floats, and no aggregate gains a disposition from this. Retyping the folds is a separate and larger question and is not smuggled in here."
 },
 "raised_by": {
  "how": "Umbrella criterion 1's emission clause, open since Phase 4 S9 and re-raised by every R-35 pass since: every disposition every production path emitted was MEASURED, so three of the four spellings were unreachable on /api/calculate, /api/bis and /api/optimize.",
  "escalation": "docs/receipts/escalated-defects-P4-S9.json, entry no_production_path_emits_a_non_measured_disposition, which retires in this commit with its reproducer inverted.",
  "what_unblocked_it": "The umbrella's Amendment E of 2026-08-14. Before it, every one of the occurrences below was a text_change R-19 sent to an investigator R-18's export could not brief, so the slice had no legal landing."
 },
 "qualifying_population": {
  "enumerated_before_the_src_edit": true,
  "enumerated_from": "scripts/golden_coupled_baseline.json (committed), by walking all thirteen scenarios for any published event row carrying a non-empty skipped_reason.",
  "rule": "Only a row the walk refused can gain a declared zero, because _refusal reads the row's own skipped_reason and _outcome is the only caller of the new verdict. The enumeration is therefore total over the committed baseline and bounds what may qualify: a moved leaf on a row with no skipped_reason, or on any field outside the three named below, is an unexpected occurrence and stops the slice.",
  "refused_rows": 24,
  "by_panel": {
   "events": 14,
   "healing_events": 10,
   "support_events": 0
  },
  "fields_a_refusal_zeroes": {
   "events": [
    "damage",
    "overkill"
   ],
   "healing_events": [
    "applied_amount"
   ],
   "support_events": [
    "applied_amount"
   ]
  },
  "why_support_events_contributes_none": "ReceiptLedger.skip zeroes applied_amount on every refusal, so a refused support row is the same shape -- the committed baseline simply holds none. The arm ships anyway, because a rule that holds only where a baseline happens to have an example is the shape this campaign removes; tests/test_program_views.py drives it directly.",
  "expected_qualifying_occurrences": 76,
  "arithmetic": "24 refused rows -> 38 refusal-zeroed outcome leaves (14x2 + 10x1) -> 38 text_change transitions on the entries' disposition strings and 38 absent_to_value transitions on the reason keys beside them."
 },
